# Mosquitto ACL for the secure broker (secure.conf). ADR-0026, REQ-SEC-004.
# One user per client role. A user that is not listed here, or a topic a user is not given,
# gets nothing: the broker drops the publish and refuses the subscription.
# Topics: spec/interfaces/topics.md (the contract, ADR-0017) plus the legacy prefixes ADR-0017 lists.

# The Pi: the API, gateways, camera service and hardware bridge. The only role that may send
# commands (vehicle/cmd/{vin}/io).
user pi-backend
topic readwrite vehicle/#
topic readwrite device/#
topic readwrite system/#
topic readwrite mia/#
topic readwrite hardware/#

# The Android app (MQTTTopics.kt): publishes telemetry, alerts, ANPR, health and sessions.
user android
topic write vehicle/telemetry/+/obd
topic write vehicle/alerts/+
topic write vehicle/events/+/anpr
topic write device/health/+
topic write device/metrics/+
topic write system/session/+

# ESP32 OBD firmware (legacy mia/ prefixes, ADR-0017).
user esp32-obd
topic write mia/telemetry/#
topic write mia/alerts/#

# The phone assistant (android-assistant mqtt_publish): lights only, which need no confirmation.
# Its confirm-class topics are refused here; a human-confirmed command goes through the Pi API.
user phone-assistant
topic write mia/lights/#
